# Age of Mortals — templates (pp.200-205).
Bound Spirit	TYPE:Acquired	VISIBLE:YES	RACETYPE:Undead	RACESUBTYPE:Incorporeal	HITDIE:12	MOVE:Fly,30	BONUS:STAT|CHA|4	BONUS:SKILL|Hide,Listen,Search,Spot|8|TYPE=Racial	LEVELADJUSTMENT:4	HD:1-3:CR:1	HD:4-7:CR:2	HD:8+:CR:3	SAB:Manifestation (Su)	SAB:Telekinesis (Su)	SAB:Frightful Visage (Su)	SAB:Magic Drain (Su)|PREHD:MIN=4	SAB:Malleable Visage (Ex)|PREHD:MIN=6	SAB:Corrupting Gaze (Su)|PREHD:MIN=8	SAB:Possession (Su)|PREHD:MIN=10	SAB:Rejuvenation (Su)	SAB:Turn Resistance +2 (+4 within 30 ft. of its vessel)	DESC:A soul bound to the mortal world (pp.200-202). Added to a living aberration, animal, beast, dragon, giant, humanoid, magical beast, monstrous humanoid or shapechanger with Charisma 6 or more; it becomes undead (incorporeal). Hit Dice d12; fly 30 feet (perfect) unless better; no Constitution; Charisma +4; +8 racial on Hide, Listen, Search and Spot. Natural armor applies only against ethereal foes; manifested, its natural armor is +0 and it gains a deflection bonus equal to its Charisma modifier (minimum +1). Its attacks harm material creatures only through special attacks when manifested. Save DCs are 10 + 1/2 HD + Charisma modifier. Telekinesis: once a round as a full-round action, as a sorcerer of its HD or 10th level, whichever is higher. Frightful visage: a free action; living creatures in a 30-foot spread make a Will save or are panicked for 2d4 rounds (a save gives a day's immunity). Magic drain (4+ HD): its touch drains 1 spell level per HD from a caster, or magical potential equal to HD + Charisma modifier from an item (Fortitude save to mitigate). Malleable visage: alter self at 6+ HD, polymorph at 12+ HD. Corrupting gaze (8+ HD): 30 feet, Fortitude or 2d10 damage and 1d4 permanent Charisma drain. Possession (10+ HD): a full-round touch while manifested; Will or possessed for 1 hour per HD as magic jar (a save gives 24 hours' immunity). Rejuvenation: destroyed, it reforms at its vessel in 2d4 days on a level check (1d20 + HD) against DC 15; only destroying the vessel first ends it. Its vessel is its own body (skull intact) or an object worth 100 gp per HD; whoever holds the vessel commands it as by control undead. It keeps 2d4 treasured items as ethereal copies; a +1 or better weapon can harm material creatures when it manifests. CR: up to 3 HD +1, 4 to 7 HD +2, 8+ HD +3; level adjustment +4.	SOURCEPAGE:p.200-202
Ogre Titan	TYPE:Acquired	VISIBLE:YES	RACETYPE:Monstrous Humanoid	RACESUBTYPE:Ogre	BONUS:STAT|STR|6	BONUS:STAT|DEX|4	BONUS:STAT|CON|4	BONUS:STAT|INT|8	BONUS:STAT|WIS|4	BONUS:STAT|CHA|10	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|4|TYPE=NaturalArmor	BONUS:SKILL|Concentration,Intimidate,Knowledge (Arcana),Knowledge (History),Sense Motive|8|TYPE=Racial	BONUS:SKILL|Listen,Search,Spot|10|TYPE=Racial	VISION:Low-light	LEVELADJUSTMENT:6	CR:2	PREALIGN:LE,NE,CE	PRERACE:1,Ogre,Minotaur,Ogre Mage,Irda,Half-Ogre	PRESTAT:1,CON=12	SAB:Elbow spurs: 2 attacks at base attack, 1d6 + Strength	SAB:Awe-Inspiring Presence (Su)	SAB:Necromantic Talent (Su)	SAB:Stone and Steel Shaping (Su)	SAB:Soul Blast (Su)	SAB:Inscrutable Intellect (Su): +6 racial bonus on saves against enchantment	SAB:Titan Language (Su)	DESC:Ogres remade by Dauroth's dark ritual (pp.203-205). Added to an ogre, minotaur, ogre mage, Irda or half-ogre with Constitution 12 or more; type becomes monstrous humanoid (ogre). Natural armor +4; two elbow-spur attacks (1d6 + Strength) at base attack. Str +6, Dex +4, Con +4, Int +8, Wis +4, Cha +10. Save DCs are 10 + 1/2 HD + Charisma modifier. Awe-inspiring presence: ogres and half-ogres (ogre magi included, not minotaurs or Irda) within 30 feet + 10 feet per Charisma modifier make a Will save or are charmed (charm person), gaining a morale bonus equal to his Charisma modifier on saves against charm and fear and on attack and damage rolls while in range; others entering make a Will save or are shaken, and panicked if he confronts them and they fail again. Necromantic talent: +4 on saves against necromantic effects (energy drain included); his necromancy spells have +2 DC and +2 on caster level checks against spell resistance. Stone and steel shaping: stone shape at will as a 9th-level sorcerer, as a full-round action with full concentration, finer work with an Intelligence check. Soul blast: at will, magic missile-like missiles of 1d4 each, each costing him hit points equal to its damage. Heightened senses: +10 racial on Listen, Search and Spot, low-light vision, darksight 30 feet. Titan language: 4 skill points to learn; understanding it by magic needs a DC 20 Intelligence check each round. +8 racial on Concentration, Intimidate, Knowledge (arcana), Knowledge (history) and Sense Motive. Alignment any evil; preferred class sorcerer; CR +2; level adjustment +6; treasure double standard. The transformation (Fortitude DC 18 or die) fades after about 28 days (sickened, then reverting within five days) unless renewed by the ritual or Dauroth's monthly elixir. A fallen titan loses the template and suffers permanent -4 Str, -6 Con, -4 Int and -8 Cha.	SOURCEPAGE:p.203-205
